= Wave 3: Stellar Dominion — Endgame Mastery

== Optimizing Production at Scale

At this stage, you control multiple sectors and stations. Optimization matters.

=== Production Ratios

Each production chain has an optimal ratio. For a self-sufficient shipyard complex:

- 1x Energy Cell production : 2x Refined Metal : 2x Hull Part : 1x Claytronics : 1x Weapon Component
- Adjust based on local workforce bonuses (each race has different efficiency).

=== Workforce Management

- Each race has different bonuses to different production types.
- Teladi: Best at refining.
- Paranid: Best at advanced electronics.
- Argon: Balanced across all types.
- Split: Best at weapon production.
- Terran: Unique production chains (computronic substrate, etc.).

Mix workforce across your stations for maximum efficiency.

== Endgame Crises

X4's endgame can trigger large-scale threats:

- _Xenon Awakening:_ Massively reinforced Xenon fleets push from all borders.
- _Faction Collapse:_ A major faction loses its last shipyard.
- _Player Threat:_ Factions may coalition against a player who owns too many sectors.

=== Surviving the Crisis

1. Maintain 3+ production stations spread across different sectors (don't put all eggs in one system).
2. Keep a mobile reserve fleet (10+ Destroyers) at your best-defended sector.
3. Have a fallback sector with self-sufficient production (closed loop).
4. Use asymmetric warfare: hit their logistics, not their fleets.

== Meta-Strategies

- _Gate Camping:_ Place laser towers at enemy gate exits.
- _Scorched Earth:_ Retreat from a sector but destroy your stations first — denies resources.
- _Economic Warfare:_ Buy all of a faction's ship-building materials before declaring war.
- _Puppet Faction:_ Keep one weak faction alive as a trading partner for blueprints.
